1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,870
The Marriage of Figaro, episode nine: Mother!

2
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:07,840
The verdict: pay her or marry her. Two thousand silver pieces, and Figaro doesn't have them.

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:17,800
One last trick: I'm a gentleman, he says. I can't marry without my noble parents' consent. Robbers stole me as a baby, dressed in gold, jewels and embroidery. And I have a mark on my arm.

4
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:25,780
A little spatula, on the right arm? asks Marcellina. How do you know? Because you are my son, Raffaello. And your father is standing right there: Doctor Bartolo.

5
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:30,750
Just then Susanna runs in with a purse: a thousand gold coins to set Figaro free.

6
00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:33,080
And she sees him hugging Marcellina.

7
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,300
Slap!

8
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:42,590
Your mother? His mother! In the famous sextet everyone explains, Susanna laughs, and Marcellina and Bartolo decide to marry as well. Two weddings today.

9
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:49,630
The Count leaves, beaten. But tonight his wife will wait for him in the garden in Susanna's dress, and Figaro knows nothing about it.

10
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,900
Next episode: the letter with the pin.
